React Flight / Next.js RCE Advisory Fix Implementation

VULNERABILITY ASSESSMENT:
This Next.js portfolio project was affected by the React Flight / Next.js RCE advisory.

ORIGINAL STATE:
- Next.js Version: 15.3.3 (VULNERABLE)
- eslint-config-next: 15.3.3 (VULNERABLE)
- React Version: 19.0.0
- React Flight Packages: None detected

VULNERABILITY DETAILS:
- Next.js 15.3.3 is in the 15.3.x range, which had an RCE vulnerability in React Flight
- According to the advisory, 15.3.x should be upgraded to 15.3.6
- The project does not use React Flight packages directly (react-server-dom-*)

CHANGES IMPLEMENTED:
1. Upgraded Next.js from 15.3.3 to 15.3.6:
   - Updated package.json: "next": "15.3.3" → "15.3.6"
   - Updated package.json: "eslint-config-next": "15.3.3" → "15.3.6"

2. Updated lockfiles:
   - Ran `npm install` to resolve dependencies
   - package-lock.json updated with patched Next.js 15.3.6 and all related packages

FINAL STATE:
✓ Next.js upgraded to patched version: 15.3.6
✓ No React Flight packages detected (none needed patching)
✓ React and React-DOM remain at 19.0.0 (managed by Next.js)
✓ All dependencies resolved correctly

VERIFICATION RESULTS:
✓ Build succeeds: `npm run build` completed successfully
✓ Linting passes: `npm run lint` with no errors or warnings
✓ Lockfile is consistent and reflects the patched versions

FILES MODIFIED:
- package.json: Updated next and eslint-config-next from 15.3.3 to 15.3.6
- package-lock.json: Updated to reflect dependency resolution with patched versions

SECURITY STATUS:
✓ Project is now protected against the React Flight / Next.js RCE advisory
✓ Using recommended patched version: Next.js 15.3.6
✓ No breaking changes introduced
✓ Build and linting verified successful
